 "intro": "In Alsace, at the foot of the Vosges, 58 BC. The German king Ariovistus has settled across the Rhine in Gaul with many thousands of warriors. You are Julius Caesar, whose army is afraid of the Germans.",
 "debrief": "In Caesar’s account, his men panicked at tales of the Germans until he said he would march with the Tenth Legion alone. German horsemen attacked his escort during a parley. Learning that German wise women forbade battle before the new moon, Caesar forced one by marching to their camp. The Germans charged too fast for pila to be thrown; when the Roman left was pressed, young Publius Crassus, commanding the cavalry, sent the third line to help. The Germans fled to the Rhine, fifteen miles away; Ariovistus escaped in a boat. The other choices are what-ifs.",
